      "writtenOn": "2026-10-20T21:42:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Architectural suggestion: `gr-vote-chip` already receives `.vote` and `.label`. If we let `gr-vote-chip` resolve AI status internally (similar to `computeClass()` and `computeTooltip()`), e.g.:\n```typescript\nprivate computeIsAi(): boolean {\n  if (this.isAi) return true;\n  return hasOnlyAiVotes(this.label, this.vote);\n}\n```\nThen:\n1. `gr-submit-requirements` wouldn\u0027t need to manually compute and pass `?is-ai\u003d${hasOnlyAiVotes(labelInfo, approvalInfo)}`.\n2. Other places using `gr-vote-chip` (such as `gr-change-list-column-requirement` in the changes dashboard table and `gr-trigger-vote`) would automatically display the AI sparkle icon for AI votes without needing separate prop plumbing.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "65c0a3f22daa795157ca59c1dd14de673a110031",
