      "writtenOn": "2026-10-20T21:42:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Having `title\u003d\"AI predicted\"` on `\u003cgr-icon\u003e` causes two issues:\n\n1. **Conflicting tooltips**: `\u003cgr-vote-chip\u003e` is wrapped in `\u003cgr-tooltip-content\u003e`, which suppresses native tooltips to display Gerrit\u0027s custom `\u003cgr-tooltip\u003e` (e.g. `\"Approved\"`). The native HTML `title` on `\u003cgr-icon\u003e` bypasses this, causing both the browser\u0027s native OS tooltip and Gerrit\u0027s custom tooltip to appear simultaneously when hovering over the icon.\n2. **Wording**: Review votes (e.g. `Code-Review +2`) cast by an AI agent are actual review approvals, not predictions (as documented in `rest-api-changes.txt`: *\"If true, this vote was created by an AI agent\"*).\n\nCould we remove `title\u003d\"AI predicted\"` from `\u003cgr-icon\u003e`, and instead incorporate the AI indicator directly into `computeTooltip()` so that hovering anywhere on the chip provides a unified tooltip? E.g.:\n\n```typescript\nconst aiSuffix \u003d this.isAi ? \u0027 (AI vote)\u0027 : \u0027\u0027;\nif (this.tooltipWithWhoVoted \u0026\u0026 this.vote) {\n  return `${this.vote?.name}: ${voteDescription}${aiSuffix}`;\n} else {\n  return `${voteDescription}${aiSuffix}`;\n}\n```",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "65c0a3f22daa795157ca59c1dd14de673a110031",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
