      "writtenOn": "2026-10-20T21:42:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we need to render `\u003cgr-icon\u003e` inside `.chip-angle`?\n\n`.chip-angle` is positioned absolute behind `.vote-chip` at `(top: 2px, left: 2px; z-index: 1)`. Because `.vote-chip` has a solid opaque background, the spark icon inside `.chip-angle` at `x\u003d2px` is completely covered and invisible to the user.\n\nAlso, `.vote-chip` includes `${this.labelName}` while `.chip-angle` does not, so if `labelName` is present, `width: auto` will size `.chip-angle` narrower than `.vote-chip`.\n\nInstead of rendering child elements and relying on `width: auto`, could we make `.chip-angle` fill the container in CSS?\n```css\n.more \u003e .chip-angle {\n  position: absolute;\n  top: 2px;\n  left: 2px;\n  width: 100%;\n  height: 100%;\n  box-sizing: border-box;\n  z-index: 1;\n}\n```\nThat way `.chip-angle` automatically mirrors the exact dimensions of `.vote-chip` without needing child DOM, and we can also add `aria-hidden\u003d\"true\"` to `.chip-angle` so screen readers don\u0027t read the vote value twice.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "65c0a3f22daa795157ca59c1dd14de673a110031",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
